  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1147 AM CST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\nA bit of an unsettled pattern for the end of the week, as a series\nof weaker shortwaves move very quickly north of the area across\nthe plains. Getting any moisture back ahead of these system back\nis going to be tough and the model blends are largely dry. A\nlittle bit of a stronger upper trough moves north of the area for\nthe weekend and the blends do show at lease some light showers\nacross portions of the area. Bigger upper level ridge follows it\nfor early next week. As for temperatures, Generally a cooler and\ndrier air mass will remain across the area with no really cold air\non the way. Lows in the 50s, and then 40s. Highs mainly in the 70s\ncooling into the 60s for the weekend.",
